#
# The morpheme table. Spec §3.3 / §3.8 / §3.9.
# Prefixes and suffixes stay in spec §3.4–§3.5 and are generated from there.
# This file adds:
#   I  present  imperative     — fill the -e form for a §3.3 root
#   R  present  supine  imperative  gloss  — extra root, insertion order
#
# Loans (whole public names that do not derive) are harvested at generation
# time from examples/, tests/programs/, tests/conformance/ by
# tools/gen-lexicon.py --harvest; they are not listed here. initium is
# reserved (§4.7) and is never a loan and never decomposed.
#
# A registered root is permanent (§3.9.4). Insertion order is load-bearing.

# §3.4: -e is the present-stem imperative, realised -e / -a / -e by
# conjugation. These fills are the forms the spec already writes in prose
# (`plica`, `lege`, `tene`) plus the regular realisations of the other
# eleven §3.3 roots. Guessing is refused in gen-lexicon.py unless listed here.
I leg lege
I scrib scribe
I sec seca
I plic plica
I numer numera
I ordin ordina
I sequ seque
I cap cape
I pon pone
I ten tene
I vert verte
I mitt mitte
I iung iunge
I solv solve

# Roots §3.3's own prose names as missing from the fourteen, and that the
# language already uses in public names. applic- enters as a root, not as
# ad- + plic- (§3.3, §3.6 would spell adplica).
R salut salutat saluta greet
R imprim impress imprime press
R applic applicat applica apply
R constru construct construe build
